---
import { SITE } from '@/config';
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="Which links earn us money, how much, and what it does and does not change about what we write."
  path="/affiliate-disclosure"
  lede="Plainly: some links pay us. Here is exactly how that works."
>
  <h2>What an affiliate link is</h2>
  <p>
    Some links to financial products — credit cards, loans, demat and investment accounts — are
    affiliate links. If you follow one and go on to open the product, the provider pays
    {' '}{SITE.name} a commission. You pay nothing extra, and the product costs you the same as it
    would if you had gone direct.
  </p>

  <h2>Where you will see it</h2>
  <p>
    Any page containing an affiliate link carries a disclosure in a box at the top, above the
    content, before you have read anything. We do not bury it in a footer.
  </p>

  <h2>What it does not change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Which products we recommend. If the right answer for you is a product that pays us nothing, or no product at all, that is what the page says.</li>
    <li>What we write about a product's drawbacks. Commission does not buy silence on fees, lock-ins or rejection rates.</li>
    <li>Which problems we cover. Pages are chosen by what readers are stuck on, not by what converts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it does change</h2>
  <p>
    It funds the site, along with advertising. Being straightforward about that is better than
    pretending this is a hobby. You should still read anything written by anyone with a commercial
    interest — including us — with that interest in mind, and check the provider's own terms before
    you apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Separately from affiliate links, the site shows ads served by third-party networks. Those are
    labelled "Advertisement". We do not choose the individual ads and their appearance here is not
    an endorsement. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for the cookies involved.
  </p>

  <p>Questions: <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
</Page>
